{"analysis":"Version 0 scored 71.6 macro-F1. The weakest label is neutral: only 118 of 207 neutral tweets were labelled neutral, with 45 going to negative and 44 to positive. A further 35 positive tweets went to neutral.

Neutral tweets called negative mostly hold mild, analytical or joking criticism rather than real upset:
- sports commentary ("Fake punt on 4th and 11? Wow", "folds up like a lawnchair", Josh Hamilton "Lol");
- political remarks (Jeb/Cantor, Kerry);
- sarcasm framed as banter;
- complaints about trivial plans (no Grey's on Thursday, dorm money, netflix tonight);
- matter-of-fact news of executions or RIP mentions.
The annotators keep these neutral unless the author is clearly angry, hurt or hostile.

Neutral tweets called positive are mostly personal plans and activities (seeing a film, going to a concert, eating deep-fried food, "who wants to come"). They get positive only with overt enthusiasm or praise.

Positive tweets called neutral are upbeat promotional or news items about something the author favours (gala, season kick-off, Apple Watch case, a team playing well, a trend listing). That direction is noisy, so I will only nudge it.

Changes for version 1:
- Raise the bar for negative to clear upset or hostility.
- Send mild critique, banter, opinionated sports analysis and trivial complaints to neutral.
- Mark tributes and memorials as positive, and plain death or execution news as neutral unless the tweet is about a violent attack.
- Require explicit emotional wording for positive on personal plans.
- Keep upbeat promotion as positive.","question":"What overall feeling does the tweet's author clearly express about its topic: positive, neutral, or negative?","rule":"Give positive or negative only when the author shows a clear feeling; when unsure, choose neutral. Mild critique, analysis, banter, sarcastic jokes among fans, sports commentary and small everyday gripes are neutral. Plans and activities stated without explicit enthusiasm are neutral, but upbeat promotion of events or products, and tributes to the dead, are positive. Real anger, insults, distress, or reports of violent attacks and killings are negative.","criteria":{"positive":{"what":"Explicit excitement, praise, love, gratitude, celebration, warm tributes, or upbeat promotion of an event, product or team.","examples":["Can't wait to see you tomorrow at The Roxy!","Celebrating the memories of a man who graced us with his knowledge and passion for the game every Monday night #RIP Frank Gifford. #Pro #NFL","Sat watching the sun set with a large glass of wine and a pack of marlies listening to fleetwood mac, DOES LIFE GET BETTER?? no, it does not"],"cues":"can't wait, excited, love, best, good, happy, thank you, fantastic, kick-off, celebrating, looking good, !!","not_for":"Plans or activities stated flatly, like going to a film or concert or asking who wants to come (neutral)."},"neutral":{"what":"News, announcements, plans, questions, opinions and commentary without strong emotion, including mild criticism, jokes, sarcasm-as-banter and small gripes.","examples":["Fake punt on 4th and 11? Wow, James Franklin can make some odd decisions. #PennState #Michigan #PSUvsMICH","Going to see Paper Towns on Saturday. I'm hoping it does the book justice.","What will happen to the clemency plea before the President? SC says Yakub can be executed on Thursday.","Kanye West is insane. He also may be a complete genius. But I still don't want him to be president. #VMAs #fb"],"cues":"may, will be, going to, who wants to, tomorrow, lol, wow, reportedly, headlines, sports scores","not_for":"Clear rage, insults or distress (negative); explicit delight or promotional hype (positive)."},"negative":{"what":"Clear anger, hatred, insults, sadness, frustration or dread, or reports of violent attacks and killings.","examples":["still so sad I'm not going to Ed Sheeran the 25th ://// ","Kanye West may in fact be the biggest douche bag in the history of the universe","Four were killed,19 injured when a IRA bomb demolished the Balmoral Furniture Building"],"cues":"hate, sad, FML, worst, bullshit, wtf, pathetic, killed, :(, :/, awkward, protest","not_for":"Analytical or joking criticism, sports second-guessing, trivial complaints about one's evening (neutral)."}}}

{"analysis":"Version 2 (68.5) leaned too far toward sentiment. Neutral recall fell to 87 of 207, with 58 neutral tweets called positive and 62 called negative. Version 0 (71.6) had the best balance, and version 1 showed that strong neutral pressure destroys negative and positive recall.

Neutral tweets called negative in version 2 were mostly:
- analytical sports or political commentary (Fake punt, Josh Hamilton, Simmons ranking, Kerry, Jeb/Cantor);
- reported news with bad elements but no author feeling (McGregor knee, Daesh warning, Boko Haram oil);
- jokey self-deprecating gripes about trivial things (no TV on Tuesday nights, netflix tonight, dorm money, put Twilight on);
- hypothetical feelings.

Neutral tweets called positive were mostly:
- personal plans and activities stated without explicit feeling words (going to a concert, eating, watching a show);
- venue or bar ads with calls to action ('Don't miss', 'Check out').

Plan for version 3:
- Start from the version 0 balance.
- Make the test whether the feeling is the point of the tweet. A clear stance or emotion gets positive or negative. Passing evaluation inside commentary, plain plans, routine ads and trivial joking gripes get neutral.
- Keep bad-news negative for real harm to people (injuries, deaths, attacks, charges) reported with concern, but not for neutral analysis.
- Avoid the over-correction of version 1 by keeping clear complaints and disappointment as negative.","question":"What overall sentiment does the tweet's author express or convey about its topic: positive, neutral, or negative?","rule":"Ask whether a feeling is the point of the tweet. Clear enthusiasm, praise, love or celebration is positive. Clear complaint, disappointment, anger, mockery, or concern about harm is negative. Neutral covers news without the author's feeling, analytical commentary on sports or politics, plain plans, routine ads ('Don't miss', 'Check out'), questions, mixed views, and trivial joking gripes.","criteria":{"positive":{"what":"Explicit excitement, happiness, praise, love, gratitude, hope or celebration, including good news the author welcomes and upbeat tributes.","examples":["Can't wait to see you tomorrow at The Roxy!","I just saw a glance at the new Galaxy Note 5. Looks interesting. That may be my next phone.","David Price is the fastest #bluejays' pitcher to reach 50Ks with the team."],"cues":"can't wait, excited, love, happy, great, good, interesting, fun, thank you, finally, celebrating, !!","not_for":"Plans or activities stated flatly, event or bar ads, 'who wants to come' questions (neutral); sarcastic praise (negative)."},"neutral":{"what":"News, schedules, plans, ads, questions, analytical commentary or opinions without strong feeling, mixed views, and light jokes or trivial gripes about one's own day.","examples":["Going to see Paper Towns on Saturday. I'm hoping it does the book justice.","Fake punt on 4th and 11? Wow, James Franklin can make some odd decisions. #PennState #Michigan #PSUvsMICH","Pretty Little Liars isn’t back on till January. What am I supposed to do with my Tuesday nights until then?","Kanye West is insane. He also may be a complete genius. But I still don't want him to be president. #VMAs #fb"],"cues":"may, will be, reportedly, going to, tomorrow, who wants to, don't miss, check out, scores, rankings","not_for":"Real complaints or disappointment (negative); explicit delight or praise (positive)."},"negative":{"what":"Clear sadness, anger, frustration, disappointment, insults, sarcasm or mockery, and reports of killings, attacks, injuries or scandals told with concern.","examples":["still so sad I'm not going to Ed Sheeran the 25th ://// ","Kanye West may in fact be the biggest douche bag in the history of the universe","Finally broke down and got Amazon Prime and the delivery on my 1st purchase as a member is late. @user I was expecting better."],"cues":"sad, bummed, hate, worst, stupid, pathetic, FML, wtf, unimpressive, frustrating, killed, :(","not_for":"Calm analysis of a team or politician, neutral news headlines, joking gripes about trivial plans (neutral)."}}}

{"analysis":"Version 3 scored 71.8, roughly level with version 0's 71.6. It fixed most neutral errors but left 57 positive tweets as neutral and 44 negative tweets as neutral.

Positive tweets missed as neutral mostly had:
- upbeat promotion of entertainment, products or media (gala, season kick-off, ticket giveaway, Apple event coverage, new Apple Watch features, National Ice Cream Day);
- achievements or recognition (Golden Globes nomination, 2nd best album, trending topic, Saudi women elected, Jays in 1st place);
- personal plans to attend concerts or fun events (on our way to Foo Fighters, AC/DC tickets for mom, Sam Smith with my sister).

Negative tweets missed as neutral mostly had:
- plain reports of violence, attacks, injuries or criminal charges (West Bank shootings, Boko Haram mastermind, Henson injury, Jenner manslaughter);
- personal mishaps or annoyances (bored and tedious, stuck in an airport, lost for 5 hours, no residual check, test tomorrow, awkward :/).

Neutral-to-sentiment errors are now low (50 in total), so I can push a little toward both sentiments in these specific areas. Analytical commentary, trivial joking gripes and flat everyday plans stay neutral.","question":"What overall sentiment does the tweet's author express or convey about its topic: positive, neutral, or negative?","rule":"Positive covers enthusiasm, praise or celebration, plus upbeat promotion of entertainment, products or media, achievements and honours, and plans to attend concerts or fun events. Negative covers complaints, disappointment, anger or mockery, personal mishaps and annoyances, and any report of violence, attacks, injuries or criminal charges, even plainly worded. Neutral covers plain news without harm or achievement, analytical commentary on sports or politics, routine logistics, questions, mixed views, and light jokes about trivial things.","criteria":{"positive":{"what":"Excitement, praise, love, hope or celebration. Also upbeat promotion of events, products or shows, achievements, nominations or rankings, and going to concerts or fun outings.","examples":["Can't wait to see you tomorrow at The Roxy!","Annual season kick-off with FENNARIO - New England's tribute to the Grateful Dead - Saturday, Aug 29th - Doors at 8pm","In the car on our way to Milton Keynes to see the Foo Fighters tomorrow. #foofighters #miltonkeynes"],"cues":"can't wait, love, excited, great, good, interesting, nomination, 1st place, kick-off, giveaway, new, live coverage, !!","not_for":"Sarcastic praise (negative); plain logistics or flat chores (neutral)."},"neutral":{"what":"News with no harm or achievement, schedules, questions, analytical opinions on teams or politicians, mixed views, and joking gripes about trivial matters.","examples":["Fake punt on 4th and 11? Wow, James Franklin can make some odd decisions. #PennState #Michigan #PSUvsMICH","Pretty Little Liars isn’t back on till January. What am I supposed to do with my Tuesday nights until then?","Kanye West is insane. He also may be a complete genius. But I still don't want him to be president. #VMAs #fb"],"cues":"may, reportedly, will be, who is going, scores, rankings, rumors, debate","not_for":"Violence, injuries or charges (negative); achievements or event hype (positive)."},"negative":{"what":"Sadness, anger, frustration, disappointment, insults, mockery, personal mishaps and annoyances, and reports of violence, attacks, injuries, crashes or charges.","examples":["still so sad I'm not going to Ed Sheeran the 25th ://// ","Day 2 stuck in the Taipei airport. Possibly going to LA to wait out the storm. Didn't think I'd make it to Cali for the 1st time this way","RT @user Gavin Henson looks set to miss the Rugby World Cup after dislocating a bone in his right wrist yesterday"],"cues":"sad, bored, tedious, stuck, lost, hate, worst, pathetic, wtf, :/, shot dead, attack, injured, charged","not_for":"Calm analysis of a team or politician, joking gripes about one's evening (neutral)."}}}
